# Every text file is LF, in the index and in the working tree, on every platform.
# git auto-detects binary content and leaves it untouched.
#
# LF is not cosmetic here: a CRLF shebang (#!/usr/bin/env node\r) makes the Unix
# kernel look for an interpreter literally named "node\r", and tooling that parses
# file content line by line misbehaves when the file and os.EOL disagree.
* text=auto eol=lf
